# Layer groups and pivot points
@scenario tutorial_lesson_48
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@character lab_card "Card" scale=0.60
@charlayer lab_card base assets/tutorial/labs/card-base.png
@charlayer lab_card strip assets/tutorial/labs/card-mark.png
@charlayer lab_card dot assets/tutorial/labs/card-dot.png
@chargroup lab_card inner pivot=0.5,0.5 $strip | $dot
@charpreset lab_card neutral $base | $inner
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/48_group_pivots.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt tilt]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: The card, strip and dot use separate PNGs on a common canvas. The strip and dot belong to one group; the backing card is separate.
@label lab
> Rotate the inner group -> tilt
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label tilt
[hide ginger]
[show lab_card guide neutral]
[if !tutorial_still]
# region tilt
timeline {
  rotate "lab_card_inner" { deg: 22 dur: 700 }
}
# endregion
[endif]
narrator: The inner group rotates together. The card backing stays fixed. Edit pivot=0.5,0.5 in this file and compare the same angle.
[hide lab_card]
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[hide lab_card]
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_48]
[flag tutorial_done_48]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_10]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Change only the group pivot. What should remain the same?
> All textures shift to a new file. -> practice_hint
> The angle and layer membership. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The group lists two layers, so both receive the transform. The backing stays fixed.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: The group lists two layers, so both receive the transform. The backing stays fixed.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: What rotates together when targeting lab_card_inner?
> The strip and the dot. -> correct
> The backing card alone. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
ginger: The group lists two layers, so both receive the transform. The backing stays fixed.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The group lists two layers, so both receive the transform. The backing stays fixed.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
